# Study for Teaching Behavioral Sciences in Schools of Medicine, Volume III: Behavioral Science Perspectives in Medical Education.

**Authors:** 

## Abstract
Volume III of a study of teaching behavioral sciences in medical school presents perspectives on medical behavioral science from the viewpoints of the several behavioral disciplines (anthropology, psychology, sociology, political science, economics, behavioral biology and medical education). In addition, there is a discussion of translating behavioral science knowledge in health skills and organizing behavioral sciences within the medical school faculties. Related documents are HE 004 788 and HE 004 789. (Author)

